context_info = ""
i = 0
for d in context:
    i = i + 1
    prompt = "You are given a single document. Extract only information relevant to this query and keep it concise.\n\nQUERY:\nWe need a movie (released before Dec 31, 2023) that matches ALL of the following:\n- It stars a Ugandan-born actor who made their screen debut in the late 1970s (circa 1975-1979) and is noted for having mastered several accents for roles across their career.\n- The film's director moved to Hollywood in the late 1980s and, as of Dec 31, 2023, had been nominated for the Oscars exactly twice.\n\nFrom the document, extract any of the following if present:\nA) Ugandan-born actor candidates: name; birth details; screen debut year/era; explicit mention of mastering several accents; notable films they starred in (title, year).\nB) Director candidates: name; evidence they moved to Hollywood in the late 1980s; count of Oscar nominations (ensure it is exactly two as of Dec 31, 2023); notable films they directed (title, year).\nC) Any explicit linkage of a candidate actor and a candidate director via a specific film (title, year).\n\nFormat your output as:\n- Document #: <number>\n- Actor candidates:\n  * <Name>: debut=<year/era>; accents=<evidence/quote>; films=[<title (year)>...]\n  Quotes: <short supporting excerpts>\n- Director candidates:\n  * <Name>: moved_to_Hollywood=<evidence>; oscar_noms=<number>; films=[<title (year)>...]\n  Quotes: <short supporting excerpts>\n- Possible matching films (actor + director both match):\n  * <title (year)>; actor=<name>; director=<name>\n\nIf the document contains none of the above, output:\n- Document #: <number>\n- No relevant information.\n\nDOCUMENT START\n" + d + "\nDOCUMENT END"
    result = llm_query(prompt)
